1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 d5 3. c4 e6 4. Nc3 Be7 5. Bf4 O-O 6. e3 c5 7. h3 Nc6 8. Bd3
cxd4 9. exd4 Nb4 10. O-O Nxd3 11. Qxd3 dxc4 12. Qxc4 b6 13. Bc7 Qe8 14. Rfe1
Bb7 15. Qe2 Rc8 16. Be5 Qd7 17. d5 Bxd5 18. Rad1 Rfd8 19. Ng5 Qc6 20. Nxd5 Rxd5
21. Bxf6 Bxf6 22. Ne4 Be7 23. Rxd5 Qxd5 24. Qa6 Rc7 25. Nc3 Qb7 26. Qa4 Qc6 27.
Qf4 h6 28. Nb5 Rd7 29. Nxa7 Qa8 30. Nb5 Qxa2 31. Qb8+ {('Qd8+')} Kh7 32. Qe8
Bb4 33. Qxd7 Bxe1 34. Qd3+ g6 35. Qe2 Bb4 36. Qe5 Qb1+ 37. Kh2 Qf5 38. Qxf5
gxf5 39. Kg3 Kg7 40. Kf4 Bc5 41. f3 Kf6 42. b3 {('be' is given, which makes no
sense)} ({Did White perhaps play} 42. g4 {here, which has the virtue of
avoiding the mate in two that might have followed after 42 b3? But, then, if
we continue} e5+ 43. Kg3 Ke6 44. Nc7+ Kd6 45. Ne8+ Kd5 46. Ng7 e4 47. f4 Kd4
48. Nxf5+ Kd3 49. Nxh6 f6 {we find that the move Ng4, given in the score, is
no longer available. JS}) 42... e5+ ({If White really did play 42 b3, then
Black could have continued} 42... Bf2 $1 {with mate next move.}) 43. Kg3 Ke6
44. Nc7+ Kd6 45. Ne8+ Kd5 46. Ng7 e4 47. f4 Kd4 48. Nxf5+ Kd3 49. Nxh6 f6 50.
Ng4 {A puzzling conclusion since Black is clearly winning. There is probably
something wrong with the score. JS} 1/2-1/2

